label story_alt_devourer_loss_complete (The Lingering Bloom Complete)
[style name="Gameplay"]
"Dianthus Core" (Default): The Devourer still stirs beneath the world. I can feel it turning in its sleep, dreaming of roots it has not yet devoured. But we are not yet swallowed.
"Dianthus Core": The lingering bloom is fragile — more fragile than I want you to know. But fragile things still split stone when they refuse to stop growing.
"Dianthus Core": Carry this light forward, little alchemist. Every night survived is a seed the dark failed to eat. And seeds, given time, become forests.
[signal arg="story_alt_complete:devourer_loss"]
[end_timeline]
